  "worked_solution": "To find the absolute value of $-7.4,$ we simply drop the negative sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∣-7.4\\,∣=7.4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of a number gives the distance between the number and zero on a number line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14145654/assets/042954891035ab9104009871bd4459aeb1e89aa95d4b2eb7d115c05b4b8ec9ba.png)",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
